From b80b6cde5a3f5b9dfe4b52c4dc443a3d2fb86df4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HMIS Patch <patch@hmis.dev>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 06:20:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(admin): add missing features to admin department

Problems fixed in this commit:

1. User model (departments/models/user.py)
   - Add email (unique, indexed) for password-reset notifications
   - Add full_name for display in user tables
   - Add is_active (soft-disable without deleting the account)
   - Add created_at timestamp (account creation audit)
   - Add last_login timestamp (populated on every successful login)

2. Database migration (migrations/versions/a1b2c3d4e5f6_...)
   - Alembic migration to ADD all five new columns to the users table
   - Includes downgrade() for safe rollback
   - Chained from latest head (fefcbf381ba9)

3. routes.py (departments/admin/routes.py)
   - AddUserForm: add full_name + email fields with Optional/Email validators
   - EditUserForm: add full_name + email + is_active BooleanField
   - add_user(): persist full_name, email, is_active; email uniqueness check
   - edit_user(): persist full_name, email, is_active; audit log includes changes
   - manage_users(): replace .all() with .paginate(per_page=25); add status
     filter (locked / inactive / no_mfa); search now covers email + full_name
   - NEW disable_mfa(user_id): admin can revoke MFA after device loss
   - NEW bulk_user_action(): activate / deactivate / lock / unlock / delete
     multiple users in one POST; skips the admin's own account
   - system_overview(): expose inactive_count; add optional psutil CPU/
     memory/disk metrics; propagate all new stats to template
   - index(): compute locked_count, mfa_count, inactive_count,
     expiring_creds_count at dashboard load

4. app.py
   - Populate user.last_login = now(utc) on successful password login
   - Populate user.last_login = now(utc) on successful MFA-verified login

5. Admin sidebar (templates/side_bars/admin.html)
   - Add links: Executive Analytics, Audit Trail, Outbound Notifications,
     Staff Credentials (were implemented but never wired into the nav)
   - Add link: Setup My MFA (mfa_setup route was orphaned)

6. Admin index dashboard (departments/admin/templates/admin/index.html)
   - Replace 3-card row with 6 metric cards: Total Users, Locked, MFA On,
     Inactive, Credentials Expiring (30 d), System Online
   - Add Quick Actions row: Analytics, Audit Trail, Notifications, Staff
     Credentials, System Logs, Setup MFA, HIPAA/Compliance, KRA eTIMS
   - All 8 previously-missing route links now surface from the dashboard

7. manage_users.html (rebuilt)
   - Pagination with iter_pages() ellipsis navigation
   - Status filter dropdown (Locked / Inactive / No MFA)
   - Search covers username + email + full_name
   - Display full_name and email beneath username
   - Display last_login column
   - Bulk-action toolbar (select-all checkbox + activate/deactivate/delete)
   - Disable MFA button per row (when MFA is enabled)

8. add_user.html (rebuilt)
   - Full Name and Email Address fields added

9. edit_user.html (rebuilt)
   - Full Name, Email, is_active toggle, last_login info strip
   - Inline Disable MFA card when MFA is active on the account

10. system_overview.html (rebuilt)
    - 6 KPI cards (adds Inactive card)
    - CPU / Memory / Disk progress-bar gauges (psutil, graceful fallback)
